USB (numeric) keypad to (USB) MIDI program and bank change translator.

Converts entries done on the keypad to MIDI program change.

- Enter program change number and press enter to send to
  connected MIDI device.
  - The number is sent directly as soon as it is complete, which
    make the Enter redundant in some cases (but pressing it
    when its not needed doesn't have any ill effects).
  - Automatically sends after 1.5s after entering digits even if
    Enter is not pressed.
  - Backspace clears the entry.
- Toggling NumLock holds the tens and hundreds, making 0..9
  directly change the units value (without pressing Enter).
  - E.g. if the current program change is 56, pressing Numlock causes
    the 5 to be held and programs 50..59 can be accessed directly
    using a single key press.
- / is a bank prefix, press / and a bank number to send
  a MIDI bank change (default CC 32) (no Enter needed).
- MIDI channel can be set by holding * and pressing 1,
  then release and follow by the channel number (1..16) and Enter.
  - This is not saved across reboots.
- Force reboot by holding * and pressing 0, release, followed
  by Del.
- By default the first program number is 0 and the first bank
  is 0, but this can be changed in cmdline.txt by setting
  program_base and bank_base to 1, respectively.
  - This changes the user view, so that if program_base
    is set to 1, then entering program change 1 will send 0 on
    MIDI. Conversely, if program_base is 0, then program change
    1 will send 1 on MIDI (and entering 0 will send 0).
    - This means that when the base is set to 1, entering 0 as
      program change value is not valid and will result in
      nothing being sent.
- The default MIDI channel is 1, but it can be changed runtime
  using the setting above, or permanently by editing
  cmdline.txt, and setting the midi_channel property.
- The default MIDI bank change CC is 32, but it can be changed
  in cmdline.txt, by setting the bank_cc property.
